Factorio AI includes third-party code:

game/client/
  The Windows and common parts of factorio-mcp by czp3009, https://github.com/czp3009/factorio-mcp (our fork's branch
  pilot as of commit e460220, 2026-11-07, which added player_action, memory_read and two world_query read forms). The
  upstream repository has no licence file; the code and its documents (tools.md, AGENTS.md, development.md, kept in
  game/client/) are used with the author's permission, relayed to us, on the condition of attribution. This project
  grants no licence to that code. Changes: Kotlin package renamed to factorioai.client, program renamed to
  factorio-ai-client.exe with factorio_ai_bridge.dll, environment variables renamed to FACTORIO_AI_CLIENT_*, the
  Linux target and npm packaging removed, local.properties generated by game/client/setup.ts.

commands/cli/
  The fh command line (compiled host/*.js) from factorio-ai-party's vendor/factorio-harness (same commit as below), MIT
  License (commands/cli/LICENSE). Changes: the --bot name rule relaxed to [A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,31} (bot names are
  model names). Our broker (commands/broker.ts) speaks its FH_SOCKET protocol; the command name stays fh because the
  reference manuals the models read use it.

training/manuals/ref/
  The reference manuals the models read with `./fh help TOPIC` (analysis, building, circuits-settings, movement-combat,
  moving-items, space-age, team, waits-queues, index.md, topics.tsv) are copied from factorio-ai-party agent/ref (commit
  a9a5556a, 2026-11-04; MIT License, see training/manuals/ref/LICENSE), unchanged except stream-people.md left out.

core/brains/hooks/
  permit.ts ports the Bash permit rules of factorio-ai-party tools/permit.py and the examples of tools/test_permit.py
  (test/permit.test.ts); context.ts and hook.ts port the Claude Code parts of tools/context.py, agent/compact.md and
  agent/context.tsv (same repository and licence as below). Changes: our own tokenizer (stricter: word-initial # only,
  unknown operators rejected, for-lists and redirect targets checked, Windows paths), our command whitelist, the wait
  rules (sleepVerdict), the read guard, lower compaction points.

game/mod/factorio-ai-harness/
  The agent-harness mod from factorio-ai-party by Nick Winter, https://github.com/nwinter/factorio-ai-party
  (vendor/factorio-harness as of commit a9a5556a, 2026-11-04; MIT License, see game/mod/factorio-ai-harness/LICENSE), itself a
  fork of factorio-harness by Carson Burke, https://github.com/CarsonBurke/factorio-harness (MIT License).
  Changes: renamed to factorio-ai-harness; ported to Factorio 2.1 (compat21.lua, defines.inventory aliases, rewritten fluidbox /
  category reads, helpers.create_profiler, a require cache so modules can be loaded as plain files, UTF-8 safe reply truncation,
  relaxed bot name rule). In this project the same Lua also runs outside the game (game/offgame/) on top of a fake game API fed
  by process memory reads; the in-game copy is only used by tests as ground truth.
  game/mod/factorio-ai-harness/rates.lua ports formulas from RateCalculator v3.3.8 by Caleb Heuer (raiguard), MIT License,
  https://codeberg.org/raiguard/RateCalculator (noted in the file).
